<ContentPage
  title="Privacy — Epub Studio"
  description="Your files are converted inside your browser and never uploaded. No accounts, no tracking, no cookies. Here is exactly what happens to your data."
  path="/privacy"
  h1="Privacy"
  lede="Your books never leave your device. This page explains exactly what that means, and what little data exists at all."
  updated="18 July 2026"
>
  <p>
    Every tool on this site runs inside your browser. When you convert a file, the work happens on
    your own machine using JavaScript this page loaded — the file is read from disk, transformed in
    memory, and handed back to you as a download. It is never sent to us, because there is nowhere
    for it to be sent to.
  </p>

  <p>
    This is not a promise about how carefully we handle uploads. It is a statement that uploads do
    not happen. You can verify it: open your browser's developer tools, switch to the Network tab,
    and convert something. You will see no request carrying your file.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>

  <p>
    Nothing. There are no accounts, no analytics, no tracking pixels, no advertising scripts and no
    cookies. We do not know who you are, what you converted, or that you were here at all.
  </p>

  <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>

  <p>Two things, both local to your browser and neither transmitted anywhere:</p>

  <h3>Style Studio settings</h3>
  <p>
    Your typeface, size, spacing and theme choices are kept in <code>sessionStorage</code> so they
    survive a page reload and apply to the next book you open. They are discarded when you close the
    tab.
  </p>

  <h3>Converted books awaiting styling</h3>
  <p>
    When a conversion produces an EPUB and you continue into Style Studio, the finished book is
    placed in <code>IndexedDB</code> so the next page can pick it up — two separate pages cannot
    share a file in memory any other way. Entries are deleted automatically after an hour, and you
    can clear them at any time through your browser's site-data settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Fonts and other assets</h2>

  <p>
    All fonts are served from this site rather than from Google Fonts or another CDN. No third party
    learns that you visited, and nothing here makes a request to a domain other than this one.
  </p>

  <h2>Formats we deliberately do not support</h2>

  <p>
    We do not convert to MOBI or AZW3. Doing so would require sending your book to a server running
    Amazon's toolchain, and we would rather not offer a tool that quietly works differently from
    every other one here. Those pages explain the alternatives instead.
  </p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>

  <p>
    This site is static files served by a host. Like any web server, that host may keep standard
    access logs — IP address, user agent, which page was requested — for operational and security
    purposes. That is a property of being on the internet at all, and it never includes anything
    about your files, because your files are never part of a request.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>

  <p>
    Data protection law gives you rights to access, correct and erase personal data held about you.
    We hold none, so there is nothing to access, correct or erase. Clearing this site's data in your
    browser removes the two local items described above.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>

  <p>
    This site is safe for anyone to use. It collects no data from any visitor, regardless of age.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>

  <p>
    If this policy ever changes, the date at the top of this page changes with it. Any change that
    weakened the core promise — that files stay on your device — would be announced on the homepage,
    not buried here.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>

  <p>
    Questions about any of this are welcome. Add your contact address here before publishing this
    site.
  </p>
</ContentPage>

